  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25145438",
      "title": "Adding Catch-All Routes",
      "lectureOrder": 237,
      "videoOrder": 221,
      "sourceHash": "8741671749818177f4fb6722d717e896ae95c1f1dad3baedb8d33c5f8537b291",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 5.1,
          "en": "Now, I did mention two extensions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.1,
          "end": 9.89,
          "en": "or variations of this concept here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.89,
          "end": 12.04,
          "en": "And the nested dynamic segments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.04,
          "end": 15.71,
          "en": "that was one important aspect of routing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.71,
          "end": 18.4,
          "en": "in Next.js when it comes to dynamic routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.4,
          "end": 21.98,
          "en": "The other important variation or extension",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.98,
          "end": 26.59,
          "en": "is that you can also define collect all routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.59,
          "end": 30.72,
          "en": "or catch all routes, and what does this mean?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.72,
          "end": 34.6,
          "en": "Let's say, we also have a blog sub folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 34.6,
          "end": 38.53,
          "en": "and now we might have different ways of loading blog posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 38.53,
          "end": 41.83,
          "en": "For example, we could get just the slug,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 41.83,
          "end": 44.06,
          "en": "just the idea of a blog post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 44.06,
          "end": 45.66,
          "en": "So therefore, of course, in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.66,
          "end": 48.85,
          "en": "we could add a file named [id].js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.85,
          "end": 52.54,
          "en": "But maybe we also want to support other URLs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.54,
          "end": 55.3,
          "en": "for loading a single blog post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.3,
          "end": 60.3,
          "en": "For example, we want a support /blog/the-id-of-a-post",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 62.91,
          "end": 65.327,
          "en": "but maybe we also want to support",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.327,
          "end": 70.327,
          "en": "/blog/2020/12/the-idea-of-a-post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 72.61,
          "end": 74.9,
          "en": "To only search for this post",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 74.9,
          "end": 78.64,
          "en": "if it was released in December 2020.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 78.64,
          "end": 83.43,
          "en": "Or we just want to load blog/2020/12",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 83.43,
          "end": 88.43,
          "en": "to load all blog posts for that specific month in that year.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 88.74,
          "end": 92.65,
          "en": "So, we have different URL formats which we want to support,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 92.65,
          "end": 94.75,
          "en": "and maybe we want to support them all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 94.75,
          "end": 98.7,
          "en": "with the same component, so no matter what the path is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 98.7,
          "end": 100.96000000000001,
          "en": "and how many segments it has",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 100.96000000000001,
          "end": 104.86,
          "en": "we always want to load the same component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 104.86,
          "end": 108.8,
          "en": "And that's what we can do with such a catch all route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 108.8,
          "end": 111.06,
          "en": "Instead of just using square brackets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 111.06,
          "end": 114.03999999999999,
          "en": "and then any identifier of our choice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 114.03999999999999,
          "end": 118.00999999999999,
          "en": "we can add a syntax here or a special notation here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 118.00999999999999,
          "end": 120.46,
          "en": "which you might know from JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 120.46,
          "end": 122.68,
          "en": "We can add three dots here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 122.68,
          "end": 125.8,
          "en": "like the spread operator in JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 125.8,
          "end": 128.87,
          "en": "And then, again, any name of your choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 128.87,
          "end": 131.64,
          "en": "So, that could be ID, that could be slug.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 131.64,
          "end": 135.91,
          "en": "I'll go for slug here but, again, that name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 135.91,
          "end": 138.73,
          "en": "The three dots are not though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 138.73,
          "end": 141.21,
          "en": "This, of course, is no special file name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 141.21,
          "end": 144.07999999999998,
          "en": "from the operating system's perspective.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 144.07999999999998,
          "end": 147.47,
          "en": "But Next.js will treat it in a special way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 147.47,
          "end": 150.96,
          "en": "just as it treats all files with square brackets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 150.96,
          "end": 153.9,
          "en": "in the file name in a special way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 153.9,
          "end": 156.44,
          "en": "So, how does it treat that file?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 156.44,
          "end": 159.93,
          "en": "Well, we still define a React component in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 159.93,
          "end": 163.46,
          "en": "so we could have the blog posts page here, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 163.46,
          "end": 165.37,
          "en": "to load all the blog posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 165.37,
          "end": 167.91,
          "en": "But then we don't know if we get, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 167.91,
          "end": 170.63,
          "en": "a path with the year and the month,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 170.63,
          "end": 175.61,
          "en": "or just with the year, or with a specific blog post already,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 175.61,
          "end": 177.99,
          "en": "or some other filter criteria,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 177.99,
          "end": 181.133,
          "en": "depending on what want to support in our page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 182.03,
          "end": 184,
          "en": "So, here, I'll return my good old div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 184,
          "end": 188.06,
          "en": "with the h1 tag of the blog posts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 188.06,
          "end": 191.023,
          "en": "and then export this as a default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 191.93,
          "end": 194.613,
          "en": "And I will already import useRouter here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 196.91,
          "end": 201.52,
          "en": "useRouter from next/router, so that we can look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 201.52,
          "end": 205.49,
          "en": "into what the next/router gives us here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 205.49,
          "end": 207.2,
          "en": "So, therefore, I'll get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 207.2,
          "end": 208.85,
          "en": "to my router by calling useRouter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 210.02,
          "end": 215.02,
          "en": "and then console.log the good old router.query value again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 215.11,
          "end": 220.11,
          "en": "like this, and if we now do that and save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 221.07999999999998,
          "end": 226.07999999999998,
          "en": "and we go to /blog/2020/12, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 227.7,
          "end": 231.13,
          "en": "you see I do load the blog posts page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 231.13,
          "end": 233.6,
          "en": "And, here, we get our query object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 233.6,
          "end": 238.6,
          "en": "with that slug property because I chose slug as a name here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 238.77,
          "end": 242.52,
          "en": "after the three dots, but the three dots are not part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 242.52,
          "end": 244.4,
          "en": "of that property name, as you can tell.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 244.4,
          "end": 248.23,
          "en": "And then, here, we get an array now and that's different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 248.23,
          "end": 252.17,
          "en": "Before we always got a single value, a single string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 252.17,
          "end": 253.97,
          "en": "Now, it's an array of strings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 253.97,
          "end": 257.45,
          "en": "for the different segments that were caught.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 257.45,
          "end": 260.08,
          "en": "So, here we caught the 2020,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 260.08,
          "end": 264.343,
          "en": "and the 12 segment separated by slashes in the URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 265.61,
          "end": 269.85,
          "en": "But because we defined this as a catch all path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 269.85,
          "end": 274.53,
          "en": "with the three dots here, next.js does catch anything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 274.53,
          "end": 278.77,
          "en": "after blog because we're defining this in the blog folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 278.77,
          "end": 282.62,
          "en": "Anything after blog is caught by this page component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 282.62,
          "end": 285.82,
          "en": "and is made available as an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 285.82,
          "end": 287.58,
          "en": "through that slug property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 287.58,
          "end": 290.253,
          "en": "on that query object in the router object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 291.15,
          "end": 293.47,
          "en": "And now we could be using these values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 293.47,
          "end": 296.87,
          "en": "to send a request to our database, to filter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 296.87,
          "end": 301.85,
          "en": "for blog posts where the year is 2020 and the month is 12.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 301.85,
          "end": 303.35,
          "en": "And, of course, you could encode",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 303.35,
          "end": 308.35,
          "en": "whatever you want here, and you get those values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 309.74,
          "end": 313.6,
          "en": "So, that's how this works and how you can utilize that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 313.6,
          "end": 315.87,
          "en": "And that's another important feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 315.87,
          "end": 318.43,
          "en": "which sometimes can become important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 318.43,
          "end": 320.79,
          "en": "and which sometimes can be helpful,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 320.79,
          "end": 324.04,
          "en": "since it allows you to write very dynamic paths,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 324.04,
          "end": 329.04,
          "en": "where not just the individual segment values are dynamic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 329.64,
          "end": 333.29,
          "en": "but even the number of segments are dynamic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 333.29,
          "end": 337.02,
          "en": "And that's not always what you need, but sometimes it is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 337.02,
          "end": 338.97,
          "en": "And therefore it is important to know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 338.97,
          "end": 342.613,
          "en": "that Next.js supports this syntax as well.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
